title: '[EPMB] bound the tx-fee refund of a signed submission'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The winner of the signed phase is paid `RewardBase` plus the transaction fees their submission cost them, tracked in `SubmissionMetadata::fee`.

    Two changes:

    - A new `signed::Config::MaxFeeRefund` caps the refundable portion, both for the winner and for an invulnerable clearing a discarded submission.
    - Storing a page that is already stored no longer accrues a fee, matching what the refund is meant to cover.

    Runtimes should set `MaxFeeRefund` to `signed::FullSubmissionFee<Runtime, TransactionPayment>`, which prices one `register` plus `Pages` `submit_page` calls at the maximum encoded page size.

    `FullSubmissionFee` needs the fee of a call it cannot afford to build, so `frame_support` gains `EstimateFee`, a sibling of `EstimateCallFee` that takes an encoded length and a `DispatchInfo` instead of a call, implemented by `pallet-transaction-payment`.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-transaction-payment
  bump: minor
